  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 234 PM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nFairly quiet weather pattern this week and currently high \npressure ridging building northward which will allow an upward trend\nin dew points and some increase in upper level clouds which \nwill help to keep lows overnight tonight a bit warmer than the \nlast couple of nights. However, our southeastern parts of the \narea the moistening will lag slightly which will allow slightly \ncooler low temperatures in that area, along with the mostly \nclear skies and light winds which will help in radiational\ncooling. This could yield some patches of frost in those \nlocations. Would recommend that if in those locales that if you\nhave some temperature sensitive plants or animals, take proper \nprecautions to protect them from the cold overnight. \n\nOtherwise, with the high pressure in place and becoming stronger\nlater this week with a high amplitude ridge building over the\ncentral CONUS. This will allow for dry weather and help to keep\nour temperatures warmer. High and low temperatures will run \nslightly above normal with values in the upper 60s to low 70s \nand lows in the 40s through the week.",
